Format1
This line, and all lines up to, but not including, the Start Data marker
are for information and not required. All other lines must be provided
in the given format, including the line with "Start Data" on it,
or the file will not be read correctly.
The routine which reads the file has very little error checking.

Y coordinate is longitudinal and X is transverse.

The fields below are required for each aircraft.

When used with LEDFAA all data values must be correct.

When used with BAKFAA only those values marked BAKFAA need
to be correct. All other fields must be present but can
have dummy values (must be at least one character long).

Aircraft Name                                      BAKFAA (for load case identification)
Gross Weight of Aircraft, lbs                      BAKFAA (load case weight)
Percent of Gross Weight on evaluation gear
Tire pressure, psi                                 BAKFAA
Gear ID letter, military designation
Gear ID number
TT, Dual Spacing, inches
TS, Gear track between inside wheels, inches
TG, Four-gear spacing, inches
B, Tandem spacing, inches
Number of tires on evaluation gear, NTires         BAKFAA
  TX TY (for NTires) in inches                     BAKFAA
Number of tire tracks, NTTrack
  XAC (for NTTracks) in inches
Number of response evaluation points, NEVPTS       BAKFAA
  EVPTX EVPTY (for NEVPTS) in inches               BAKFAA


